      "role": "user",
      "content": "Okay, that makes more sense. So the displacement field is basically just describing how the electric field is distributed in that space? \n\nI'm still a bit confused about the dielectric part though. If the plates are separated by an insulator, how does that \"displacement\" actually help store more charge? Does the dielectric material itself do something to the field that makes the capacitor more effective?",
